Yes, randomly generated objects are a key source
of enchant weapon scrolls, specifically.  That's why
there aren't always a whole lot of them -- because
randomly generated objects may be a main source
of scrolls of enchant weapon, but they are not the
main source of scrolls in general.

This and several other scrolls that do not occur much
in monster equipment are the main reasons a magic
marker is almost never a waste of a wish.

> While you, OTOH, seem to be focussing on
> monster equipment, which contributes to a huge
> degree to only a _specific subset_ of all objects. -

Monsters contribute the overwhelming majority
of all objects in the dungeon, period.  Items that
do not occur (or do not occur very often) in monster
inventory are, as a rule, at least semi-rare, unless
they have a huge probability within their item class
or are guaranteed in some other way.

> I think those are two different topics.

Perhaps, but the two topics are related.

> Scrolls of enchant weapon are (AFAIK) never
> part of the monster equipment.

Exactly.  That's why you never  have more than a
few of them, unless you polypile (or engage in
extensive farming, which just generates a ton
of items in general).

> But they are generated as [random] death-drops,

Random death drops are probably the main source
of random object generation, but as near as I can
tell they average less than one item per monster.
Monster inventory averages somewhere in the
neighborhood of half a dozen items per monster,
give or take a bit, depending on what kinds of
monsters you're getting (which partially depends
on role and experience level, as well as dungeon
branch and level).

> as [random] objects in shops

I discussed that upthread.  The only scroll that
has a high enough probability to occur in large
numbers because of shops is the scroll of identify.

> [random] contents of containers.

Yes, typically 3-5 random items per container
(sometimes fewer or even none, occasionally
more, but we're approximating here), average
about 2 containers per level if the RNG is your
best friend for life, fewer otherwise.  That makes
about half a dozen items per level, give or take.
This is not entirely insignificant, but it's small in
comparison to monster inventory.

> where scrolls are involved. Typically this scroll
